    "cons": [
      "Remote access depends on buying and setting up the bridge accessory",
      "Fingerprint readers can be fussy with wet, dirty or worn fingertips"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The pick for households that want to unlock the door with a finger, as long as you accept the extra bridge for remote access.",
    "description": "The U-Bolt Pro is for anyone who has stood on a porch with full hands and no keys. It combines a fingerprint reader, a keypad, Bluetooth app control and a physical key override in one deadbolt, so there is almost always a way in. For remote lock control and alerts, Ultraloq offers a separate Wi-Fi bridge accessory rather than building the radio in, which keeps the lock's own battery use lower but adds a purchase and a plug-in device. Fingerprint capacity and enrollment are straightforward, and the manufacturer lists support for common voice assistants. The main caveat is the usual one for biometrics: owners commonly mention that wet or dirty fingers can fail to read, so keep the keypad code as a backup. It is a sensible choice when ease of entry matters more than a polished ecosystem."
