        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          A smart lock is only worth owning if it still works on the worst day: dead batteries, a router outage, a guest with no app. The best smart lock is the one that fits your door, matches the way your household actually enters the house, and fails gracefully. Here are the seven we would consider for a real front door, and exactly who each one is for.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="what-a-smart-lock-does" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. What a Smart Lock Actually Does (and What It Does Not)
          </h2>

          <p>
            A smart lock is a deadbolt with a motor, a radio and a battery pack. It does the same mechanical job as the lock it replaces: a bolt slides into your door frame. The difference is how it decides to move. Instead of a key turning a cylinder, a code on a keypad, a fingerprint, a tap from a phone or a command from an app tells a small motor to throw the bolt. That sounds modest, and it is, but the practical effect on daily life is large. You stop carrying a key, you stop hiding a spare under a planter, and you stop wondering whether you locked the door after you left.
          </p>

          <p>
            The honest way to think about the category is as convenience first, security second. A good smart lock is not meaningfully harder to break through than the quality deadbolt it replaces, because the strength of a door comes from the bolt, the strike plate, the frame and the screws holding them together. What a smart lock adds is control: you can give a dog walker a code that works only on weekday afternoons, delete it when the arrangement ends, and see who came and went. For anyone who has ever had to rekey a house after a lost key, that alone pays for the lock.
          </p>

          <p>
            It is worth being clear about what the category does not do. A smart lock does not make a weak door strong, and it does not replace a camera or an alarm. If your front door is a hollow slab with a short strike plate screwed into a thin frame, the lock is not the weak point. Pair a lock with a <a href="/best-home-security-cameras/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold hover:underline">good security camera</a> or a <a href="/best-video-doorbell/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold hover:underline">video doorbell</a> and you get the other half of the picture, the footage that shows who was at the door when the log says it opened.
          </p>

          <p>
            This guide follows the format of our other buyer's guides, and we want to be plain about its basis. We have not run bench tests on these locks, so you will not find invented measurements below. What you will find is the manufacturer's published specifications, what owners commonly report, and our reasoning about which lock suits which house. Where a detail varies by model or region, we say so and tell you what to check on the listing before you buy. For the bigger picture of how a lock fits into a sensible upgrade budget, see our <a href="/home-improvement-ideas/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold hover:underline">home improvement ideas</a> guide.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. The 7 Best Smart Locks in 2026, Ranked
          </h2>

          <p>
            We ranked these seven on how well they suit a real front door: how they are installed, how you get in without a phone, and what happens when the batteries run low. We have not bench tested them, so the notes below draw on manufacturer specifications and what owners commonly report. The Check Price buttons are affiliate links, so we earn a commission if you buy through them, at no extra cost to you.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
              <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
